fact WorkItem(id: "WI-085", description: some(value: "anthill-todo CLI: 'add' generates duplicate IDs (WI-001 instead of next sequential) when the workitems.anthill file has a parse error. Root cause was upstream of the CLI: the tree-sitter grammar's string_literal regex /\"[^\"]*\"/ rejected backslash-escaped sequences, so any string containing \\\" (which the printer emits to encode embedded quotes) failed to parse. The whole file's parsed view collapsed, leaving zero WorkItems in the KB and the CLI's next-id logic falling back to WI-001. Same root cause produced 'WorkItem sort not found in KB' for files that combined embedded quotes with em-dashes. Fixed: (1) tree-sitter grammar string_literal regex now accepts /\"([^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"/ and grammar regenerated, (2) parse/convert.rs decodes escape sequences (\\\", \\\\, \\n, \\r, \\t) into the resulting Literal::String, (3) added persistence_test::round_trip_escapes_preserve_content and round_trip_entity_with_string_fields_preserves_escapes regression tests covering term-source-term round-trip with quotes / backslashes / em-dashes / control chars in both positional-arg facts and named-arg entity-shaped facts. Verified end-to-end: lf1 webots dir loads, anthill-todo add now allocates next sequential id even with quotes and em-dashes in the description."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Verified(at: "2026-04-25T19:19:29Z"))
